    {
      "name": "VrfProofCommit",
      "docs": [
        "One per VRF call. Stores a cryptographic commitment to the proof bytes.",
        "The actual proof is held off-chain by the operator (in DB or wherever);",
        "what lives on-chain is `sha256(proof_bytes)`, plus convenience hashes of",
        "the memo and alpha for verifiers.",
        "",
        "Stored as a Light compressed PDA. Seeds:",
        "[\"vrf_proof\", authority_pda_pubkey, memo_hash]",
        "",
        "Memo collision within an authority is impossible because `memo_hash` is",
        "part of the seed (also gives free replay protection)."
      ],
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "authority",
            "type": "pubkey"
          },
          {
            "name": "memo_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "proof_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "alpha_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "committed_slot",
            "type": "u64"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "VrfProofCommitWithBeta",
      "docs": [
        "Same address namespace as `VrfProofCommit`, but also stores the 64-byte",
        "`beta` output of `vrfProofToHash`. With `beta` on-chain, other Solana",
        "programs can read the random value directly via a Light SDK CPI without",
        "needing the original proof bytes off-chain.",
        "",
        "Trust model is identical to `VrfProofCommit`: anyone can later audit that",
        "the stored `beta` matches `vrfProofToHash(proof)` and that the proof",
        "satisfies ECVRF — but a consuming program reading on-chain trusts that",
        "the operator (whose pk is frozen in `VrfAuthority`) populated it",
        "correctly.",
        "",
        "Seeds: [\"vrf_proof\", authority_pda_pubkey, memo_hash]"
      ],
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "authority",
            "type": "pubkey"
          },
          {
            "name": "memo_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "proof_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "alpha_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "beta_lo",
            "docs": [
              "First 32 bytes of the 64-byte beta. The split is the RC1 layout; the",
              "account is hashed flat (sha256 of its borsh bytes), not per field."
            ],
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "beta_hi",
            "docs": [
              "Second 32 bytes of the 64-byte beta."
            ],
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "committed_slot",
            "type": "u64"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "VrfProofCommitted",
      "docs": [
        "Event-mode commitment emitted by `commit_proof_event`. Unlike `VrfProofCommit`,",
        "this never creates a compressed PDA — it just lives in the transaction log.",
        "",
        "Off-chain verifiers reconstruct the authority address from `(owner, label)`",
        "using the same seed derivation as a `VrfAuthority`, then look up the",
        "authority's compressed PDA for the published pk / suite / frozen state.",
        "",
        "Replay protection is moved from the chain to the verifier: an operator",
        "could emit two events with the same `memo_hash` and different",
        "`proof_hash`es. ECVRF output is unique per (pk, alpha): every proof that",
        "verifies yields the same beta, so duplicates cannot change the result;",
        "verifiers match `proof_hash` against the proof they hold."
      ],
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "owner",
            "docs": [
              "The signer who emitted this commit. Implicitly the authority owner —",
              "off-chain verifiers re-derive the authority address from (owner, label)."
            ],
            "type": "pubkey"
          },
          {
            "name": "label",
            "docs": [
              "32-byte authority label, matches the seed used by `VrfAuthority`."
            ],
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "memo_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "proof_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "alpha_hash",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "committed_slot",
            "type": "u64"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "VrfRootRing",
      "docs": [
        "The last 128 batch roots of one authority, readable by other programs without CPI.",
        "Entry `seq` lives at `entries[seq % 128]` and is live iff `seq != 0 && entries[seq % 128].seq == seq`.",
        "Seeds: [\"root_ring\", authority_address]. 7,352 bytes with the discriminator."
      ],
      "serialization": "bytemuck",
      "repr": {
        "kind": "c"
      },
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "version",
            "type": "u8"
          },
          {
            "name": "bump",
            "type": "u8"
          },
          {
            "name": "capacity",
            "type": "u16"
          },
          {
            "name": "_pad",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                4
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "next_seq",
            "docs": [
              "Sequence the next commit must claim; starts at 1."
            ],
            "type": "u64"
          },
          {
            "name": "authority",
            "docs": [
              "The authority's compressed-account address."
            ],
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "owner",
            "type": "pubkey"
          },
          {
            "name": "label",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "reserved",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                64
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "entries",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                {
                  "defined": {
